**Finding submitted: LOL-CAP — missing (critical).**

**Investigation.** I read the entire agreement (sec-p0000, sec-p0001, sec-1.4, sec-5.4, sec-p0072) and ran targeted searches for "liability", "damages", "aggregate", "indemnif", "limitation", "disclaim", "exceed", "consequential", "in no event" and "lost profits". The only responsive hits are:
- 10.2 No Joint Venture (p0061–p0062) — agency/partnership liability only, not a cap;
- 4.2(a) Termination Payment (p0026) — "aggregate Net Sales", a pricing formula, not a liability cap.

Section 9 (Warranties) contains only mutual authority representations and the Globix acknowledgement — no hidden cap or damages waiver — and Section 10 (General Provisions) runs from notices to headings without any liability language. There is no indemnity clause and no defined "Fees"/"Losses" term (Section 3 payments are 30% of Net Sales).

**Classification.** No usable clause exists anywhere, so every fallback element fails: no cap at all (both parties, including the Company, are exposed to unlimited liability and consequential damages) and no carve-outs. This is not a case of vendor-favourable drafting we can trim — it is a genuine gap, so I drafted fresh at the preferred level rather than downgrading.

**Redline (validated ok:true).** A single `insert_after` at p0070 adding Section 10.9, placed inside Section 10 so it survives two years under 10.7:
- mutual aggregate cap at the greater of fees paid or payable by the Company in the 12 months preceding the event and USD 1,000,000;
- mutual waiver of indirect, incidental, special and consequential damages;
- uncapped "Excluded Claims" covering confidentiality, data protection and security breaches, indemnification obligations, gross negligence, willful misconduct, fraud and infringement of the other Party's IP;
- the Company's payment obligations are not damages subject to the cap.

All eleven preferred elements are mapped to that one operation; the comment states the position and offers the 12-month fee-cap fallback.
